# Push Notification Templates and Sending

## Complete Structure

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';
import { Expose } from 'class-transformer';
import { IsString } from 'class-validator';
import {
  IPushNotificationMessage,
  PushNotificationService,
  RegisterPushNotificationTemplate,
} from '~common/push-notifications';

// Template Data Class
export class FeaturePushNotificationTemplateData {
  @Expose()
  @IsString()
  name!: string;
}

// Template Provider Service
@Injectable()
export class FeaturePushNotificationService {
  constructor(private readonly pushNotificationService: PushNotificationService) {}

  @RegisterPushNotificationTemplate({
    template: {
      name: 'feature-notification',
      notification: {
        title: 'Hello, {{name}}!',
        body: 'This is a notification for {{name}}',
      },
    },
    validate: FeaturePushNotificationTemplateData,
  })
  featureNotification(message: IPushNotificationMessage): IPushNotificationMessage {
    // Optional: preprocess message before sending
    return message;
  }
}
```

## Implementation Rules

### File Organization
- File: `{feature}.push-notification.service.ts`
- Contains: Template data class and service class with template methods

### Template Data Class
- Use `@Expose()` and validation decorators (`@IsString()`, `@IsNumber()`, etc.)
- Properties: `readonly` with `!` for required, `?` for optional
- Property names must match template variables (`{{variableName}}`)

### Template Definition
- **name**: Unique identifier (kebab-case)
- **notification.title**: Notification title (supports `{{variable}}`)
- **notification.body**: Notification body (supports `{{variable}}`)
- **notification.imageUrl**: Optional image URL (supports `{{variable}}`)

### Template Provider Service
- Must be `@Injectable()` class
- Inject `PushNotificationService` in constructor
- Methods decorated with `@RegisterPushNotificationTemplate()`
- Receives `IPushNotificationMessage`, returns `IPushNotificationMessage`
- Can preprocess message before sending
- Register in module providers

### Sending Push Notifications

```typescript
import { PushNotificationService } from '~common/push-notifications';

await this.pushNotificationService.sendMessagesTemplate(
  {
    resourceName: userId, // Send to all tokens for this resource
    // or tokens: ['token1', 'token2'], // Send to specific tokens
  },
  'feature-notification', // Template name
  {
    name: 'John Doe',
  },
);
```

### Module Registration

```typescript
@Module({
  imports: [PushNotificationModule.forFeature([/* plugins */])],
  providers: [FeaturePushNotificationService],
})
```
